{#
    This template builds a Python dictionary named 'contract' in memory.
    Keys are only added to this dictionary if the corresponding data exists and is not null.
    At the end, the entire dictionary is converted to a JSON string.
    This ensures that missing data results in the key-value pair being omitted
    entirely, guaranteeing valid JSON output without comma-handling issues.
#}
